The Mind-Energy law states that mental energy scales inversely with the third power of the perceptual time threshold:
E_m = \frac{1}{\tau^3}
The threshold \tau is the shortest interval within which two stimuli are still experienced as one moment. The exponent 3 is not a free parameter: it follows from the assumption that the perceptual field can divide along three independent directions, and that energy per direction runs linearly with the sampling rate 1/\tau.

